station-goal-expedition =
    NanoTrasen management is dissatisfied with the loss of several objects in your sector and requests that expedition teams investigate these incidents.
    Your shift's goal is to complete five successful expeditions to planets with a "high" difficulty rating and prepare a report for each trip using the "Expedition Report" form.
    Assemble a volunteer team consisting of:
    salvage specialists as the team's primary firepower;
    a scientist and a doctor.
    For safety reasons, medical and scientific personnel are strictly forbidden from engaging with potential threats.
    After each expedition, the expedition scientist must complete the "Expedition Report" form, then have the Quartermaster stamp it.
    After all requested expeditions have been completed, fax the reports stamped by the Quartermaster to Central Command.
station-goal-guests =
    Your shift's goal is to prepare to receive highly important guests.
    You must renovate the station's service department.
    To do so, upgrade the kitchen by installing at least two additional microwaves and two blenders, improved by R&D, and expand the order pickup area.
    Restore the old bar by installing a counter, an alcohol dispenser, a non-alcoholic drink dispenser, and a booze-o-mat.
    To complete the assignment, chefs and bartenders must each prepare at least ten complex dishes and ten shaker-made drinks, then place them in the fridge.
    After completing the renovations, fill out the "Service Department Renovation Report" and fax it to Central Command.
station-goal-saveplanet =
    A disaster has struck planet {$rand_planet_name}.
    Your station is the closest station to the planet, so your shift has been assigned to provide emergency assistance.
    Your shift's goal is to build a remotely piloted shuttle and stock it with supplies.
    An atmosphere and gravity are not required because the shuttle will not be used to evacuate the planet's population. It does not need to be large; a shuttle measuring 9x6 tiles, excluding engines, is sufficient.
    Complete the "Emergency Aid Manifest" form, leave it inside the shuttle, and fax a copy to Central Command.
    Stock the shuttle with the following supplies:
    - 30 bicardine tablets
    - 30 dermaline tablets
    - 30 inaprovaline tablets
    - 30 dylovene tablets
    - 30 iron tablets
    - 30 chironalin tablets
    - 20 rations consisting of food and non-alcoholic drinks (their contents may vary or be identical)
    - 3 autonomous traction mechanized units (Ripley) fitted with hydraulic clamps
